Subject: [PATCH 6/6] F635-8: a carried push's PushBackDamage written as a
 damage table (data 16.635.3)

Data 16.635.3 writes BattleRam_EV1_PushBack's PushBackDamage 83 as a damage table, {BaseDamage 83,
Flags NoCounter}. The carried push reads either form: the number, or the table's BaseDamage with
no flag or NoCounter; another field or flag is refused. What NoCounter turns off is not read from
the game (b): the 16.402.x push's hit takes no hit id from the battle's counter, and the flag is
read as keeping the hit as the number form dealt it.
ActionRowsTest: the carried push test reads either shipped form; a new test holds both table forms
and the refusals (red on the number-only read).
Core tests: 16.402.22 2150/0; 16.635.3 (guard bypassed for the run) 3 -> 0 failures.
---
 .../crforge/core/battle/data/ActionRows.java  | 40 ++++++++++++++-
 .../core/battle/data/ActionRowsTest.java      | 51 ++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 89 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/src/main/java/org/crforge/core/battle/data/ActionRows.java b/core/src/main/java/org/crforge/core/battle/data/ActionRows.java
